A||N||9||MooCow||Are Fiero's a good car to buy or not??||||5
Z||000000||MooCow||09-21-1999||10:29 PM||||I was wondering how reliable Fiero's are because I'm looking at an 86 SE loaded with everything auto with the car being gold.<BR>They are asking $3,000 for it and it has 88,000 miles on it.  Is that a good deal?  Any and all info would help greatly.||||reg||5
Z||000001||chris6878||09-21-1999||10:31 PM||||Sounds Like a good deal to me... go for it...  drive it first and see how you like the feel of a fiero...  but trust me.. you will like it.<P>chris||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||09-22-1999||05:45 AM||||I guess that it really depends on what your definition of "good" is.  You do have to realize that all Fieros are over 10 yrs old.  Alot can happen in those years, and without knowing the exact history of the car, you will be taking a risk that it was mistreated at some time in its life.  There are a lot of quirks with the Fiero, it is not your typical car, but that is also one reason why it is so appealing.  Those that can do alot of the repair work themselves will probably enjoy the fiero more than those that pay mechanics by the hour.<BR>  It is reasuring to note that many of these cars have over 200k miles with no body rust, and the entire body can be replaced with basic tools if needed. <P>Mike<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||09-22-1999||06:48 AM||||If you don't do your own work on your cars, then a fiero is probably not for you.  Unless you are VERY financially stable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> If you do work on them, its a terrific car.  You simply can't buy anything else for under $3500 with this kinda performance.  ||||reg||4
Z||000004||AL||09-23-1999||01:39 AM||||well let me say this, if you are anxious to buy,then buy it. but if your not then keep lookin,i looked for a year and finally found an 86gt for 900.the body was sound the interior is perfect,it had a scratch here and there, but it worked fine. i took the heads off and took them to the shop,it cost me 150.i did allthe sevices(cap rotor wires spark plugs belts tranny and the radiator cleaned) now it's all put back together and that car drives sweet.all for a grand total of 1500 hundred. so you see if you wait you can find better, but if you can't and you like it, go for it. fiero's get in your blood so beware, and good luck.||||reg||7
Z||000005||AL||09-23-1999||01:41 AM||||i forgot to mention my car had 73.000 miles on it when i bought it.it now has 73.230 on it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pat||09-23-1999||02:51 AM||||Get the "original" 84! or look for a 88' with a V-8. I heard that are kinda fast.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||09-23-1999||08:43 AM||||$3000 sounds like a little too much for an 86 SE with 88K, unless it's in absolutely immaculate condition.  But it would probably make a good daily driver - I think the V6's are marginally more reliable than the 4-bangers, and the auto trans means you won't have to screw around with clutch service like most of the rest of us!||||reg||1
Z||000008||BOILERMAKER||09-23-1999||09:05 AM||||I just looked at a silver 85/86 SE yesterday.  I asked what year it was and the guy told me it as a '90......  hummmmmmm??  I had to laugh, but I tried to restrain myself.  He also didn't have the key to the trunk and claimed that he couldn't get in.  When I hit the autopop for the trunklid he started asking how in the hell I did that. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Point of the story is.  he wanted around 1600 for the car and I don't even think it was worth that.  It was pretty ragged out, but did have a 6cyl in it.||||reg||7
Z||000009||88 Fiero||09-23-1999||10:42 AM||||MW...is right!!! the cars are over 10 yrs. old and maintaining it and reliability will always be a question...Chad is right too!!! I paid $3,000 on my '88 Formula 5-speed. At that time my car got 73,000 miles and I am the second owner.. I was lucky because the guy took very good care of it...The inside of the car still smells brand new...I am not kidding...I own the car for 4 yrs. now and it has 83,000 miles on it...The car is most of the time....{=o)||||reg||1
